## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to architect a Redux-like store with optimistic UI updates and per-room scope. It probes how a candidate manages derived data (unread count, last messages) using memoized selectors, implements React.memo for efficient list rendering, and handles cleanup of async operations when switching contexts.

## Key Concepts
- useReducer + Context for a minimal Redux-like store
- Optimistic UI patterns with rollback on failure
- Memoized selectors keyed by roomId using useMemo
- React.memo for performant list item rendering
- Cleanup of timeouts and subscriptions on room changes

## Code Example
